console.error observed once during the evaluation session (non-deterministic, could not
reliably reproduce with repeated fresh navigations to "/" afterward — tried 3x, 0/3 repro).

First observed: appeared in the console history (level=error, all=true query) after the
AC6 push-to-talk hold/release test. Exact triggering navigation not pinpointed; most
likely candidate is one of the earlier full-page reloads where the crash-report opt-in
dialog (OptInDialog / CrashReportSection) is server-rendered without knowledge of prior
client dismissal state, causing an SSR/CSR mismatch during hydration of +layout.svelte.

