Followed by an un-leveled duplicate entry with the same TypeError stack (browser console
often logs the caught hydration failure twice: once as the SvelteKit dev-mode warning,
once as the underlying thrown error).

Assessment: this error is scoped to +layout.svelte / root layout hydration, not to any
voice-input component (VoiceInputSection.svelte, ChatInput.svelte, voiceInput.svelte.ts,
pttKey.ts). It appears app-shell-wide and pre-existing-likely rather than caused by the
voice-input feature branch. However, per the evaluator's strict PASS gate
("console.log に error レベルのメッセージが 0件"), its mere presence during the session
blocks an automated-verification PASS regardless of causal attribution. Reported here for
transparency; recommend triage as a separate defect (possibly OptInDialog SSR/CSR state
mismatch) rather than blocking this feature's acceptance criteria substantively.
